{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'ladder-cost|article-candidates' /Users/lchingen/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md; cat clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/ladder-cost/article-candidates.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"v4\": {\n  \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\",\n  \"period\": \"2026, due 2027-12-31\",\n  \"candidates\": [\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Microsoft's Azure cloud business is reported to carry a staggering $627 billion in remaining commercial performance obligations (RPO).\",\n     \"Microsoft's Azure cloud business carries approximately $627 billion in remaining commercial performance obligations, per the article — a backlog figure for a large AI hyperscaler and Nvidia customer.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:b680fbe2c3e9228eba33a0b4\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Startup activates nuclear microreactor live on stage to power an Nvidia RTX Spark desktop PC — firm working with Nvidia to build a 30MW closed loop AI factory that doesn’t use local water\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Tom's Hardware reports that public opposition to data centers in the US — with 7 out of 10 Americans saying they do not want a data center in their backyard — led to the delay or cancellation of at least 75 data center projects in the first quarter of 2026, citing power and utility cost increases, w\",\n     \"Community pushback against data centers, with 7 out of 10 Americans saying they do not want a data center in their backyard, led to the delay or cancellation of at least 75 data-center projects in the first quarter of 2026, according to the article.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:bf158d067256a39f02f7c7ce\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA Unveils New AI Compute Model, But Michael Burry is Shorting Its Stock\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"In its market-wrap section, the item reports that Meta's US$145 billion AI spending plan put chip stocks in focus this week; no period for the spending plan is stated.\",\n     \"The item cites a US$145 billion AI spending plan by Meta, framed as a factor putting chip stocks in focus; no period or data-center capex breakdown is given.\",\n     \"mitrade.com's market-wrap note cites Meta's US$145 billion AI spending plan, saying it puts chip stocks in focus; the item does not state the period the plan covers or break out how much is data-center capital expenditure.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-04\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"According to fool.com, the four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend about $650 billion on data center capital expenditures in 2026 (\\\"this year\\\").\",\n     \"The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in 2026, according to the article's account (no source cited for the plan).\",\n     \"The four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures in 2026 (referred to in the item as \\\"this year\\\"), per the fool.com article, which cites no individual company disclosures.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"24/7 Wall St. noted that hyperscalers are now having to move into debt and equity offerings and that whether growth slows dramatically in 2028 is now a central investor question, while it judged demand strong in 2027.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"A Utah microreactor just powered an Nvidia AI chip live on stage, a first for next-generation nuclear in America, and the two companies used the moment to announce a 30-megawatt AI factory in the desert designed to drink zero local water\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"More than 75 US data-center projects worth around $130 billion have been blocked or delayed across the US so far this year, according to a running tally at Tom's Hardware, and polling cited in the same reporting found 7 out of 10 Americans do not want a data center built near their home. The item fr\",\n     \"More than 75 US data center projects worth around $130 billion have been blocked or delayed so far in 2026, according to a running tally at Tom's Hardware cited by autonocion.com, and polling in the same reporting has 7 out of 10 Americans saying they do not want a data center built near their home.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 — Is Micron the new Nvidia?\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031, for cumulative spending of about $7.6 trillion from 2026 through 2031; the spending spans chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking and related infrastructu\",\n     \"Goldman Sachs estimates that annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031, with cumulative spending of about $7.6 trillion from 2026 through 2031, covering chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking and related infrastructure.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:6ab3379f10dfeb28924ebb57\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA DSX Promises More Revenue per Gigawatt. Who Actually Captures It?\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang has said a 1-gigawatt AI factory that once cost $20–30 billion now runs $50–60 billion and will soon reach $80–100 billion per gigawatt, with 100 gigawatts expected online before the end of the decade.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Below $200 Per Share Again. Here's When It Could Hit $300.\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"NVIDIA management, on its most recent quarterly conference call, forecast that hyperscaler spending will top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026, per this report by Keithen Drury of fool.com.\",\n     \"On its most recent quarterly conference call, NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending would reach a projected $650 billion in 2026 and then top $1 trillion in 2027.\",\n     \"On NVIDIA's most recent quarterly conference call, NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending will top $1 trillion in 2027, after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026. Reported by Keithen Drury in fool.com.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Morgan Stanley Research estimates that Nvidia's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation — nearly double generation over generation.\",\n     \"Morgan Stanley Research, in a bill-of-materials analysis reported by MarketScale, estimates that Nvidia's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers about $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation, i.e. the overall system price nea\",\n     \"Morgan Stanley notes, in the analysis reported by MarketScale, that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the Vera Rubin rack price down to around $6.7 million, a reminder that procurement structure materially moves the per-rack number.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"v5\": {\n  \"question\": \"How will server DRAM and HBM contract prices in calendar 2027 compare with calendar 2026?\",\n  \"period\": \"2027, due 2028-01-31\",\n  \"candidates\": [\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:82efe7d37ce9286b38e5aac5\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia’s Silent AI Colonialism Is Trapping East Asia in a Fossil-Fueled Hell - The Diplomat – Asia-Pacific Current Affairs Magazine\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Samsung and SK Hynix, which the article says produce most of Nvidia's memory chips, are pursuing massive expansions to meet surging chip demand, and both are key partners in South Korea's 'Yongin Mega-cluster' semiconductor fab and AI-factory complex. The item gives no size or date for the memory ca\",\n     \"Samsung and SK Hynix — the two South Korean manufacturers that produce most of Nvidia's memory chips — are pursuing massive memory-chip production expansions to meet surging chip demand.\",\n     \"The article reports that Samsung and SK Hynix, which produce most of Nvidia's memory chips, are pursuing large expansions to meet surging chip demand and are key partners in the South Korean government's \\\"Yongin Mega-cluster\\\" plan, a complex of semiconductor fabs and AI factories that the article sa\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:3faf8050f6d3b8ddee1d18c2\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA’s RTX 3060 12 GB Graphics Card Comeback Proves Just How Bad Things Are For The PC Gaming Market\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"wccftech reports that the DRAM crisis is intensifying in 2026 and that graphics-card prices continue to rise across all commodity memory, including the GDDR7 used in NVIDIA's RTX 50 GPUs. The outlet states that DRAM manufacturers have locked in multi-year and long-term agreements and are committing \",\n     \"Wccftech reports that as the DRAM crisis intensifies in 2026, graphics card prices continue to rise and prices for components and products have swollen sharply over the past few months, with participants signaling a further intensification of this trend in coming years.\",\n     \"Wccftech says DRAM manufacturers have locked in multi-year and long-term agreements and are promising to pour billions of dollars into new manufacturing facilities built only to meet AI demand, which it believes means the memory crisis will not end soon and the consumer market will not be relieved.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Micron reported fiscal Q3 revenue rose 345.7% year over year to $41.46 billion, and CEO Sanjay Mehrotra cited multi-year Strategic Customer Agreements meant to lock in durability, per 24/7 Wall St.\",\n     \"Micron forecast adjusted gross margin of 86% for its next quarter, a level the article notes is above the peak gross margin NVIDIA has ever achieved.\",\n     \"Some estimates cited by 24/7 Wall St. put half of all data-center spending going toward memory in 2027.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 — Is Micron the new Nvidia?\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Micron reported fiscal Q3 2026 revenue of $41.46 billion, up from $9.30 billion a year earlier (about 346% growth); GAAP net income of $28.24 billion versus $1.89 billion; gross margin of 84.6% versus 37.7%; and operating margin of 80.4% versus 23.3%.\",\n     \"Apple said it can no longer absorb the surge in memory and storage costs and announced price increases for some Macs and iPads, citing higher memory costs.\",\n     \"Micron Technology, a memory supplier, reported for its fiscal third quarter of 2026 revenue of $41.46 billion versus $9.30 billion a year earlier (about 346% growth), GAAP net income of $28.24 billion versus $1.89 billion, GAAP gross margin of 84.6% versus 37.7%, and operating margin of 80.4% versus\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Chinese firms leave Nvidia for local AI suppliers, survey shows\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"A Bloomberg Intelligence report warned that a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to benefit, and that bottlenecks are shifting from computing power to securing supply of high-bandwidth memory chips.\",\n     \"The Bloomberg Intelligence report said a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like SMIC, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to benefit, and that bottlenecks are shifting from sheer computing power to securing supply of high-bandwidth memory (HBM) chips.\",\n     \"The Bloomberg Intelligence report said a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to benefit, as bottlenecks shift from sheer computing power to securing supply of high-bandwidth memory chips.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Morgan Stanley estimates memory content per Vera Rubin VR200 rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND; memory's share of the bill of materials rose from 5-10% on the \",\n     \"The article reports that contract DDR5 pricing has climbed sharply and that device makers including Samsung and Apple are expected to pass higher memory costs into upcoming products, attributing the pressure to constrained supply of DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory against AI-driven demand.\",\n     \"Morgan Stanley estimates memory content per Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more of 3D NAND. As a share of the bill of materials, memory rose from 5–10% \"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Can Micron Technology Become the New Nvidia?\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Micron said that 'tight market conditions' in memory could last until 2028, indicating a prolonged memory shortage beyond the near term. Attributed to Micron's recent quarterly announcement as reported by the article; no specific date given.\",\n     \"The article states that new memory capacity for many in the industry will not be online until 2027 or later, keeping supply low for at least the next year and a half and potentially pushing memory chip prices even higher as demand does not slow. Presented as the author's forecast, not a company figu\",\n     \"Micron Technology, in its most recent quarterly announcement, said that tight memory market conditions could last until 2028, according to the Fool.com column.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:1b5a3359dd0644861c0fce42\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-08\",\n    \"title\": \"BofA Sees Nvidia at $350: The Market May Be Pricing In Too Much Fear\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"BofA estimates that HBM content per rack could rise by about $0.2 million to $0.3 million in the move from Blackwell to Rubin, while total rack pricing could increase by $2 million to $3 million, from roughly $3 million to $4 million for