    \"title\": \"NVIDIA's New Liquid-Cooled Data Centers Are Running At An Unexpected Temperature\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"In a blog post by Josh Parker, Nvidia's head of corporate sustainability, Nvidia announced that its DSX AI factories are hosting Nvidia's Rubin AI infrastructure with no fans or cold aisles as part of a 100% liquid-cooled design. The item does not quantify Rubin shipments or revenue, but indicates R\",\n     \"NVIDIA, in a blog post attributed to its head of corporate sustainability Josh Parker, announced that its DSX AI factories are hosting its Rubin AI infrastructure in a fully liquid-cooled configuration with no fans or cold aisles.\",\n     \"Nvidia, in a blog post by Josh Parker, its head of corporate sustainability, announced that Nvidia DSX AI factories are hosting Nvidia's Rubin AI infrastructure with no fans or cold aisles, using pure liquid cooling in which coolant enters the chip at 45 degrees Celsius and exits at 55 degrees; Nvid\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"AMD Stock and Intel Crushed Nvidia in the First Half. Here's My Prediction for the Second Half.\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"According to the article, Nvidia is launching its first-ever stand-alone CPU this fall (2026) as part of its Vera Rubin platform.\",\n     \"Nvidia is launching its first-ever stand-alone CPU this fall (fall 2026) as part of the Vera Rubin platform, per the article.\",\n     \"Nvidia is launching its first-ever stand-alone CPU in fall 2026 as part of the Vera Rubin platform, as reported by Fool.com's Adria Cimino.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"According to the report, Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\",\n     \"Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud, according to the report.\",\n     \"Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and will begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"24/7 Wall St. reported NVIDIA shares were under pressure on reports of delays across the upcoming lineup of its Vera Rubin server systems; the reports are attributed to unnamed sources.\",\n     \"24/7 Wall St reported that NVIDIA shares were under pressure on reports of delays across NVIDIA's upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems; the item cites unnamed reports and specifies neither which products are delayed nor by how long.\",\n     \"The article reports that NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across its upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Jim Cramer Says Buy Nvidia as Chipmaker Rejects 2028 AI Delay Claims\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Nvidia rejected SemiAnalysis's claims that its Kyber NVL144/Rubin Ultra rack timeline has slipped, telling media outlets that its product roadmap remains intact.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"The article stated that the reported Kyber delay applies only to the Rubin Ultra phase and its Kyber rack; Nvidia's 2026 Rubin GPUs, which reuse the current Oberon rack, are not part of the reported delay.\",\n     \"An Nvidia representative responded to Tom's Hardware's questions about the reported Kyber delay with the statement \\\"Our roadmap is intact,\\\" providing no further details; the article noted it is unclear whether this refers to the original roadmap and delivery schedules or to a revised roadmap.\",\n     \"An Nvidia representative told Tom's Hardware, in a short statement, \\\"Our roadmap is intact,\\\" and provided no further details in response to follow-up questions; the article states it is unclear whether this refers to the original roadmap, planned delivery schedules and hardware, or to an already-upd\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Delays Next-Generation Kyber Server Architecture as Manufacturing Hurdles Give Rivals a Rare Opening\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and are set to start shipping in fall 2026 to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud, according to the article.\",\n     \"Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are reported to be in full production and set to start shipping in fall 2026 to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\",\n     \"The article reports that Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and are set to start shipping this fall (calendar 2026) to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia underperforms peers as report sparks rack delay worries\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"An Nvidia spokesperson, in a brief statement emailed to Investing.com, refuted the SemiAnalysis delay allegations, saying \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\",\n     \"An Nvidia spokesperson refuted SemiAnalysis's delay claims in a statement emailed to Investing.com, saying \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"v8\": {\n  \"question\": \"Will Chinese authorities issue any authorization for Chinese companies to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027?\",\n  \"period\": \"2027, due 2027-01-31\",\n  \"candidates\": [\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:a6ed98dfdf1ad76f6edffdfd\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Singapore seizes $42m mansion over Nvidia chip smuggling\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"The BBC reports that the US has since approved the sale of some of Nvidia's semiconductors to China, under certain conditions.\",\n     \"The BBC reports that the US has since approved the sale of some of Nvidia's semiconductors to China, under certain conditions, following Washington's 2022 restrictions on exports of the chips.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:f8d63eab0337895e8e95cf02\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Uses The Specter of Huawei to Make Its Chip Exports Case\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"President Trump announced that his administration would allow Nvidia to sell its H200 chips to China last December, after the U.S. government had previously restricted such sales under Biden-era export controls on the chip (launched in 2023).\",\n     \"The Chinese government has to date locked Nvidia out of the China market, despite the Trump administration having cleared the path for H200 exports.\",\n     \"President Trump announced last December (2025) that his administration would allow NVIDIA to sell its H200 chips to China, reversing prior restrictions the Biden administration had imposed on the chip (launched in 2023) under export controls.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia’s Biggest Threat Is This: Everyone Is Desperate to Stop Paying Nvidia Prices.\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said China data center compute revenue is effectively zero and that losing the market, which NVIDIA sizes at close to about $50 billion in the future, would be material, as reported by 24/7 Wall St.\",\n     \"NVIDIA's China data center compute revenue is effectively zero, and CFO Colette Kress said losing that market — which NVIDIA sizes at close to about $50 billion in the future — would be material.\",\n     \"NVIDIA's China data center compute revenue is effectively zero, and CFO Colette Kress said losing that market — which NVIDIA sizes at \\\"close to about $50 billion in the future\\\" — would be material.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:8d5c91ae833af14257a59b2b\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Chinese firms leave Nvidia for local AI suppliers, survey shows\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"The article reports that Beijing has urged Chinese technology firms not to use Nvidia's H20 chips; the survey cites this restriction, still in force, as one reason Nvidia's China position is eroding.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"DeepSeek develops AI chips, challenging Nvidia and Huawei\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile said Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way, and that DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology; he added the DeepSeek chip development woul\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-08\",\n    \"title\": \"China to let AI firms buy Nvidia H200s, says report\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Chinese officials have told Alibaba Group, ByteDance and DeepSeek they will be permitted to buy limited quantities of Nvidia's H200 AI processors, on condition the companies state how many chips they need and why, according to The Information on July 8, which cited two unidentified people familiar w\",\n     \"US President Donald Trump granted Nvidia permission to sell H200 processors to China in December, but Chinese authorities have been slow to let the technology into the country, according to The Straits Times.\",\n     \"In May, Nvidia chief financial officer Colette Kress said the H200 chips had yet to generate any revenue for the company in China, and said Nvidia was uncertain whether any imports would be allowed into the country.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-08\",\n    \"title\": \"Chinese companies are ditching Nvidia’s advanced accelerators for domestic AI suppliers\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"According to the Bloomberg article, Beijing has urged Chinese tech firms not to use NVIDIA's H20 chips, a policy stance the item reports as being in force.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:50a84fa6b2f3eb33f29948a4\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"The Download: a nuclear landmark, and China eyes Nvidia chips\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"MIT Technology Review's 9 July 2026 Download newsletter, citing The Information, reported that China plans to let its top AI firms buy Nvidia H200 chips, naming Alibaba, ByteDance and DeepSeek as set to receive permission. The permission is reported, not announced by Chinese authorities.\",\n     \"MIT Technology Review's Download newsletter, citing Reuters, noted that China had previously withheld approval for imports of Nvidia H200 chips despite the chips being authorized for export by the United States, describing the regulatory position that the reported new permission would change.\",\n     \"The Information reported, in an item relayed by MIT Technology Review's The Download, that China plans to let its top AI firms — Alibaba, ByteDance and DeepSeek — buy Nvidia H200 chips and that they are set to receive permission. The report describes a planned step by Chinese authorities, not an iss\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Bears Add to Wagers as Competition Threatens Its Dominance: Short Seller Tracker\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"China is moving to grant limited approval for domestic firms to purchase NVIDIA H200 processors, but companies must now request individual approval for specific quantities and use cases, according to the item.\",\n     \"China is moving to grant limited approval for domestic firms to purchase Nvidia H200 processors, with companies now required to request individual approval for specific quantities and use cases, according to the report.\",\n     \"China is moving to grant limited approval for domestic firms to purchase Nvidia H200 processors, with companies required to request individual approval for specific quantities and use cases.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:91684b863d274b10246d0c13\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"Game-changer? Why China is finally letting its AI firms buy the Nvidia H200\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"The US government (Washington) approved Nvidia's H200 graphics processing unit for export to China in early 2026, a rare step, as reported by the South China Morning Post.\",\n     \"Beijing has deliberately restricted Chinese firms from purchasing Nvidia's H200 GPUs as part of its technology self-sufficiency drive, the South China Morning Post reported.\",\n     \"China's government plans to let selected companies, including Alibaba Group Holding, buy limited numbers of Nvidia's H200 GPU, a change in its stance, a source with knowledge of the matter told the South China Morning Post.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"v9\": {\n  \"question\": \"What total amount of financing commitments and capacity backstops to customers and partners will NVIDIA report outstanding at its FY2027 year-end?\",\n  \"period\": \"FY2027, due 2027-02-28\",\n  \"candidates\": [\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"NVIDIA published a statement on its official website on July 1 announcing a new business model that combines revenue sharing with credit support, enabling AI cloud providers to procure NVIDIA infrastructure without bearing the full upfront capital expenditure and to offer computing services to downs\",\n     \"The Information reported that NVIDIA is providing financial guarantees to young cloud service providers that lease or rent its GPUs: if these companies fail to secure enough AI developers to rent their computing capacity, NVIDIA will repurchase their unsold GPU capacity at a pre-agreed price; in ret\",\n     \"According to a regulatory filing NVIDIA submitted in May of this year (covering the quarter ended in April), NVIDIA added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:87607a311ad24b410c6ef85a\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n    \"title\": \"Intel Price Forecast: Nvidia Picked Xeon 6, Invested $5B, Yet Analysts Still Trail INTC\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"NVIDIA invested $5 billion of equity in Intel (NASDAQ: INTC), a transaction TradingKey's July 1, 2026 article treats as one of the two central catalysts of the Intel investment case and describes elsewhere as an equity commitment; the item gives no date for the investment itself.\",\n     \"NVIDIA made a $5 billion equity investment in Intel, which the article also describes as NVIDIA's \\\"$5 billion equity commitment\\\" and lists among the commitments underpinning Intel's story; the item gives no date, terms, stake size or completion status, and no consideration is stated.\",\n     \"NVIDIA invested $5 billion of equity in Intel Corporation; TradingKey presents the stake, alongside NVIDIA's selection of Intel's Xeon 6 as host CPU for DGX Rubin NVL8 systems, as a core catalyst for Intel's mid-2026 re-rating. The item gives no date for the investment and does not state whether the\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:cdd5ccd6fd57b79e703bfb7d\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia offers revenue sharing model for aspiring AI start-ups\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Nvidia Corp, in a blog post by CFO Colette Kress, introduced a revenue-sharing model under which it will grant token credits to developers in exchange for a share of their future sales, aimed at researchers and early-stage companies that lack capital for large-scale AI resources. Kress said Nvidia w\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"nvblog:nvidia-unlocks-ai-compute-at-scale-capital-partners-to-power-ai-infrastructure-buildout\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA Unlocks AI Compute at Scale, Inviting Partners to Power the AI Infrastructure Buildout | NVIDIA Blog\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"NVIDIA announced it is introducing a new business model under which AI clouds procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through a revenue-sharing and credit-support model; under the partnership the AI clouds sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services while NVIDIA earns both s\",\n     \"NVIDIA announced a new business model under which AI clouds procure NVIDIA infrastructure through a revenue-sharing and credit-support arrangement; the AI clouds sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, and NVIDIA earns standard product revenue plus a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity,\",\n     \"NVIDIA announced it is introducing a new business model in which AI clouds procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through a revenue-sharing and credit-support arrangement; AI clouds sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product reven\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:3854aeddaa3f31de00cf2816\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia offers to take a cut of AI cloud revenue on top of hardware sales in new optional financing vehicle — trades tokens for revenue cut\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"NVIDIA announced a new \\\"revenue-sharing and credit-support model\\\" in a blog post co-authored by CFO Colette Kress: partner AI clouds procure NVIDIA infrastructure and sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, and NVIDIA collects its usual hardware product revenue plus a percentage of the cloud income earn\",\n     \"Sharon AI separately holds a revenue-share facility of up to $200 million with investor Digital Alpha, disclosed in its CY25 results, meaning portions of its income are now pledged in two directions (to Digital Alpha and to NVIDIA's revenue-sharing model).\",\n     \"NVIDIA announced a new 'revenue-sharing and credit-support model' in a blog post co-authored by CFO Colette Kress: partner AI clouds buy NVIDIA infrastructure and sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, and NVIDIA collects its usual hardware product revenue plus a percentage of the cloud income earned o\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:bf158d067256a39f02f7c7ce\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA Unveils New AI Compute Model, But Michael Burry is Shorting Its Stock\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"NVIDIA unveiled a new AI compute framework under which cloud providers can deploy advanced hardware using revenue-sharing and credit-support agreements, aiming to lower infrastructure barriers for startups, enterprises, model developers and regional AI operators; NVIDIA earns revenue from hardware s\",\n     \"NVIDIA announced a new AI compute framework that lets cloud providers deploy advanced hardware using revenue-sharing and credit-support agreements, with NVIDIA earning revenue from hardware sales and from cloud usage generated by the supported capacity; the aim is to reduce infrastructure barriers a\",\n     \"NVIDIA announced a new AI compute framework under which cloud providers can deploy NVIDIA hardware through revenue-sharing and credit-support agreements, with the stated goal of reducing infrastructure barriers for startups, enterprises, model developers and regional AI operators; NVIDIA earns reven\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia acts as backstop for customer GPUs in return for cut of cloud revenue\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Nvidia is acting as a financial backstop for neocloud customers buying its AI chips, agreeing to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate in exchange for a share of the customers' cloud revenue, per a company post detailing the new offering. Nvidia said the model lets AI clouds procure Nvidia infrastru\",\n     \"NVIDIA announced a new revenue-sharing and credit-support model under which it acts as a financial backstop for neocloud customers buying its AI chips: it agrees to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate in exchange for a share of the customers' cloud revenue, and in the partnership AI clouds sell Nv\",\n     \"Nvidia announced a new model under which it acts as a financial backstop for AI-cloud (neocloud) companies in exchange for a share of their revenue, agreeing to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate. In a post describing the offering, Nvidia said the model lets AI clouds procure Nvidia infrastructur\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:dde08c03c8dd6f66031632d5\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia launches revenue-sharing model for AI startups\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Nvidia announced on Wednesday a revenue-sharing program that gives AI startups, model builders and enterprises access to its computing infrastructure without financing hardware buildouts themselves; under the arrangement revenue from both product sales and cloud operations flows back to Nvidia as AI\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-03\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Launches GPU Backstop Financing Model, Takes Cut of Cloud Revenue From Neocloud Partners\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"On July 1, 2026, Nvidia unveiled a financing vehicle it calls the \\\"AI Compute Partnership,\\\" under which it acts as a financial backstop for neocloud customers' GPU deployments and in return takes a recurring share of the cloud revenue those GPUs generate. Under the structure Nvidia guarantees a floo\",\n     \"NVIDIA on July 1, 2026 unveiled a financing vehicle it calls the \\\"AI Compute Partnership\\\" under which it acts as financial backstop for neocloud customers' GPU deployments: it guarantees a floor utilization rate on deployed GPUs and, if a partner's customer demand falls short, commits to renting the\",\n     \"On July 1, 2026 Nvidia unveiled a financing vehicle it calls the \\\"AI Compute Partnership,\\\" under which it acts as a financial backstop for neocloud customers' GPU deployments and takes a recurring share of the cloud revenue generated on that capacity. Under the program, Nvidia guarantees a floor uti\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:1e7a9c953f3ad70093b67ae4\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-04\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia introduces revenue-sharing model for AI cloud financing\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"NVIDIA unveiled a revenue-sharing financing model under which AI cloud operators can procure NVIDIA infrastructure with credit support, with revenue sharing linked to the cloud services sold on that capacity; NVIDIA receives its standard product revenue from the infrastructure sale plus a share of t\",\n     \"NVIDIA launched a revenue-sharing financing model for AI cloud providers under which operators can procure NVIDIA infrastructure with credit support, with revenue sharing linked to the cloud services sold on that capacity; NVIDIA receives its standard product revenue from infrastructure sales plus a\",\n     \"Nvidia unveiled a revenue-sharing financing model under which AI cloud operators can procure Nvidia infrastructure with credit support, with revenue sharing linked to the cloud services sold on that capacity. Nvidia receives its standard product revenue from the infrastructure sales plus a share of \"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"v13\": {\n  \"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n  \"period\": \"2027, due 2028-12-31\",\n  \"candidates\": [\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:bf158d067256a39f02f7c7ce\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA Unveils New AI Compute Model, But Michael Burry is Shorting Its Stock\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"In its market-wrap section, the item reports that Meta's US$145 billion AI spending plan put chip stocks in focus this week; no period for the spending plan is stated.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-04\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Nvidia projects that the big four AI hyperscalers' data center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion next year (2027), according to fool.com, following the roughly $650 billion planned for 2026.\",\n     \"NVIDIA projects that the big four AI hyperscalers' data-center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion next year (calendar 2027), up from the roughly $650 billion planned for 2026.\",\n     \"Nvidia projects that the big four AI hyperscalers' data center capital expenditures, about $650 billion in 2026, could reach $1 trillion next year (2027), according to the fool.com article.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"24/7 Wall St. noted that hyperscalers are now having to move into debt and equity offerings and that whether growth slows dramatically in 2028 is now a central investor question, while it judged demand strong in 2027.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"A Utah microreactor just powered an Nvidia AI chip live on stage, a first for next-generation nuclear in America, and the two companies used the moment to announce a 30-megawatt AI factory in the desert designed to drink zero local water\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"More than 75 US data-center projects worth around $130 billion have been blocked or delayed across the US so far this year, according to a running tally at Tom's Hardware, and polling cited in the same reporting found 7 out of 10 Americans do not want a data center built near their home. The item fr\",\n     \"More than 75 US data center projects worth around $130 billion have been blocked or delayed so far in 2026, according to a running tally at Tom's Hardware cited by autonocion.com, and polling in the same reporting has 7 out of 10 Americans saying they do not want a data center built near their home.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 — Is Micron the new Nvidia?\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Goldman Sachs estimates that annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031, with cumulative spending of about $7.6 trillion from 2026 through 2031, covering chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking and related infrastructure.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:6ab3379f10dfeb28924ebb57\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA DSX Promises More Revenue per Gigawatt. Who Actually Captures It?\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang has said a 1-gigawatt AI factory that once cost $20–30 billion now runs $50–60 billion and will soon reach $80–100 billion per gigawatt, with 100 gigawatts expected online before the end of the decade.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Below $200 Per Share Again. Here's When It Could Hit $300.\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"NVIDIA management, on its most recent quarterly conference call, forecast that hyperscaler spending will top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026, per this report by Keithen Drury of fool.com.\",\n     \"On its most recent quarterly conference call, NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending would reach a projected $650 billion in 2026 and then top $1 trillion in 2027.\",\n     \"On NVIDIA's most recent quarterly conference call, NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending will top $1 trillion in 2027, after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026. Reported by Keithen Drury in fool.com.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Morgan Stanley Research estimates that Nvidia's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation — nearly double generation over generation.\",\n     \"Morgan Stanley Research, in a bill-of-materials analysis reported by MarketScale, estimates that Nvidia's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers about $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation, i.e. the overall system price nea\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Can Micron Technology Become the New Nvidia?\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"The article states that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026 ('this year'), and that next year (2027) that figure could be over $1 trillion, which it says will drive higher demand for memory chips and for Nvidia GPUs. Reported as an aggregat\",\n     \"The same Fool.com column stated that next year (calendar 2027) AI hyperscaler data-center capital expenditures 'could be over $1 trillion', up from $650 billion this year.\",\n     \"The article states that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in 2026 (this year), and that next year (2027) that figure could exceed $1 trillion.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"According to the article, Nvidia claims the big four AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data-center capital expenditures next year (calendar 2027), versus around $650 billion planned for 2026. This is a forecast attributed to Nvidia, not a reported actual spending figure.\",\n     \"Nvidia claims that next year (calendar 2027) this group of big-four AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data-center capital expenditures.\",\n     \"NVIDIA claims the big four AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data-center capital expenditures next year (2027).\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"v16\": {\n  \"question\": \"How much will cloud providers spend on custom AI silicon (ASICs) in calendar 2026?\",\n  \"period\": \"2026, due 2027-03-31\",\n  \"candidates\": [\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:87607a311ad24b410c6ef85a\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n    \"title\": \"Intel Price Forecast: Nvidia Picked Xeon 6, Invested $5B, Yet Analysts Still Trail INTC\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Google signed a multiyear deal, announced with its Q1 2026 results, to keep using Intel Xeon processors in its workload-optimized instances, including Xeon 6 in its C4 and N4 instances, and is co-developing custom ASIC Infrastructure Processing Unit (IPU) chips with Intel; Intel CEO Lip-Bu Tan said \",\n     \"Google signed a multiyear agreement with Intel for continued use of Intel Xeon processors in Google's workload-optimized instances, including the newest Xeon 6 processors that power C4 and N4 instances, and the two companies are co-developing custom-designed ASIC Infrastructure Processing Unit (IPU)\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Bloomberg Intelligence, cited by 24/7 Wall St., forecast a 27% compound annual growth rate for custom AI ASICs through 2033, versus 16% for AI accelerators, as Broadcom's custom ASICs for Alphabet and Meta gain traction.\",\n     \"Broadcom guided third-quarter AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year, per 24/7 Wall St.\",\n     \"Broadcom guided its fiscal Q3 AI semiconductor revenue to $16.0 billion, more than 200% year over year, per 24/7 Wall St; the item does not state the fiscal year of that Q3.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:4d1b1ca014068fb532f116b3\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia’s Biggest Threat Is This: Everyone Is Desperate to Stop Paying Nvidia Prices.\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Amazon has disclosed that its Trainium custom AI chip business is now a multi-billion-dollar business, per 24/7 Wall St.\",\n     \"Amazon has disclosed that its in-house Trainium AI chip business is now a multi-billion-dollar business; the article notes that every hyperscaler funding NVIDIA's data center segment also funds an alternative to NVIDIA.\",\n     \"Amazon has disclosed that Trainium, its in-house AI chip, is now a multi-billion-dollar business; the author notes every hyperscaler funding NVIDIA's data center segment also funds an alternative.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"DeepSeek develops AI chips, challenging Nvidia and Huawei\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, 'last month' in collaboration with Broadcom, part of a broader trend of major AI companies developing their own chips.\",\n     \"The article places DeepSeek within a broader trend of major AI companies developing their own chips, noting that OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, last month in collaboration with Broadcom, and that Anthropic is reportedly considering developing its own AI chips.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"A Circuit Board Problem Just Delayed Nvidia's Next AI System to 2028 And Chip Stocks Are Already Feeling the Fallout\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Broadcom reported Q2 AI semiconductor revenue of $10.8 billion, up 143% year over year, and guided Q3 to $16.0 billion.\",\n     \"Google reported Google Cloud revenue rose 63%, with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion, and guided 2026 capital expenditures up to $190 billion; the item frames the strong cloud results as strengthening its in-house TPU case.\",\n     \"Bloomberg Intelligence forecasts a 27% compound annual growth rate for the custom ASIC market through 2033.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:3ea4e94c707ece2db2d7caec\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia is a victim of the compute marketplace it created\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"TechCrunch's Russell Brandom reported that Google, Amazon, Microsoft and OpenAI have launched their own custom AI processors to lessen their dependence on Nvidia, and said that even where those chips are not as good as Nvidia's latest model they are good enough to drive down the price of compute.\",\n     \"Google, Amazon, Microsoft and OpenAI have launched their own custom AI processors to lessen their dependence on Nvidia; even if less capable than Nvidia's latest chips, they are good enough to drive down the price of compute, TechCrunch reports.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia owns the AI chips market. Google, Amazon, and others are coming\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Google announced its newest custom AI chip, Ironwood, earlier in 2026; the inference chip is available to rent to Google Cloud customers in North America and Europe, and Google can link up to 9,216 Ironwood chips in a cluster.\",\n     \"Amazon's Annapurna Labs announced that Trainium3, the fourth generation of its AI training chips, went on sale in December 2025.\",\n     \"Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2, the prior generation, had no spare capacity left to sell and had grown into a multibillion-dollar business at a 150% quarterly clip.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Bears Add to Wagers as Competition Threatens Its Dominance: Short Seller Tracker\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Reuters reported Thursday, citing Meta Platforms' internal memo, that Meta is planning to start manufacturing its own AI chip in September, working with Broadcom to design it and Taiwan Semiconductor to manufacture it, as Meta seeks to compete with Amazon, Microsoft and Alphabet in AI cloud services\",\n     \"Meta Platforms is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its own AI chip in September, working with Broadcom on design and TSMC on manufacturing, according to a Reuters report citing Meta's internal memo.\",\n     \"Meta Platforms is reportedly planning to start manufacturing its own AI chip in September 2026, working with Broadcom to design it and Taiwan Semiconductor to manufacture it, according to a Reuters report citing an internal company memo. The report notes Meta is Nvidia's fifth-largest customer, behi\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:86c243945145ed901feb26cf\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-09\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's nearly $1 trillion wipeout could prompt this bullish action\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya, in a note this week, cited competition from custom ASIC chips among the concerns fueling Nvidia's sell-off.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:09b9d76297a57f198651c5e7\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-10\",\n    \"title\": \"What's Going On With Nvidia Stock Friday\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Reuters reported that Meta Platforms plans to begin manufacturing its custom AI processor, code-named Iris, in September after completing initial testing. The chip is being designed with Broadcom and manufactured by TSMC, and the report said it is intended to support Meta's AI infrastructure while c\",\n     \"Reuters reported that Meta Platforms plans to begin manufacturing its in-house AI processor, code-named Iris, in September after completing initial testing, with the chip designed with Broadcom and manufactured by Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing; the report said the processor is intended to suppo\",\n     \"Reuters reported that Meta Platforms plans to begin manufacturing its custom AI processor, code-named Iris, in September after completing initial testing; the chip is being designed with Broadcom and manufactured by TSMC, and is intended to support Meta's AI infrastructure while complementing, rathe\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"v18\": {\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Rubin Ultra generation, in Kyber NVL144 racks, by December 31, 2027?\",\n  \"period\": \"2027, due 2027-12-31\",\n  \"candidates\": [\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Research firm SemiAnalysis said in a post on Monday that Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 rack architecture — the rack-scale system slated to debut with the Vera Rubin Ultra generation in 2027 — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, because the PCB midplane at the heart of the system remains difficu\",\n     \"Nvidia rejected SemiAnalysis's report that the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028, stating, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\",\n     \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia's backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together to reach similar compute power was cancelled after cloud service providers and hyperscalers rejected the design as awkward and operationally burdensome, leaving Nvidia, in the firm's words, with \\\"no proven \"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"24/7 Wall St reported that NVIDIA shares were under pressure on reports of delays across NVIDIA's upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems; the item cites unnamed reports and specifies neither which products are delayed nor by how long.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Jim Cramer Says Buy Nvidia as Chipmaker Rejects 2028 AI Delay Claims\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Research firm SemiAnalysis claimed that Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 high-density rack architecture — the design built for Rubin Ultra GPUs and showcased at GTC earlier in 2026 — has slipped by more than 12 months, blaming persistent manufacturing problems with the system's complex PCB midplane. Nvidia sub\",\n     \"Nvidia rejected SemiAnalysis's delay claims, telling media outlets that its roadmap remains intact.\",\n     \"Research firm SemiAnalysis alleged that Nvidia's high-density Kyber NVL144 rack architecture, built for Rubin Ultra GPUs, has slipped by more than 12 months, blaming persistent manufacturing problems with the system's complex PCB midplane, and also claimed Nvidia scrapped its NVL72x2 back-to-back ra\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Analyst firm SemiAnalysis reported on X that Nvidia's next-generation AI server rack system, Kyber NVL144, has been pushed back more than twelve months to 2028 because of manufacturing problems, as reported by the-decoder.com. According to SemiAnalysis, the problem is the circuit boards: the PCB mid\",\n     \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia's planned alternative server design, NVL72x2, which would have placed two Oberon racks back to back, has been scrapped entirely, after cloud providers and large data center operators pushed back against the unusual form factor and the high operational overhead.\",\n     \"SemiAnalysis reported that the more powerful four-compute-die version of Nvidia's upcoming Rubin Ultra chip has been canceled, and only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia pushes Kyber release to 2028 following manufacturing concerns – report\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia has delayed production of its Kyber rack-scale architecture by more than 12 months, pushing its release date to 2028 from an originally planned 2027, citing manufacturability problems with the printed circuit board (PCB) midplane that connects the modules.\",\n     \"SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia's alternative plan to place two Oberon racks back-to-back to achieve similar power output has been scrapped after cloud companies and hyperscalers pushed back against its 'odd design and heavy operational burden.'\",\n     \"SemiAnalysis reported that the manufacturing issues will also impact the planned NVL576 system, which connects 8x Oberon racks over CPO between the NVSwitches, likely delaying it or limiting it to small volumes, and said Nvidia is left with 'no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for R\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:c0432377817a1c00a1bbadf0\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia AI server delay report sends Asian tech stocks sliding\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Research firm SemiAnalysis said in an X post that Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 next-generation AI server rack system has been delayed by more than a year due to manufacturing difficulties, specifically setbacks in the construction of printed circuit boards for the platform. Nvidia did not respond to a requ\",\n     \"Research firm SemiAnalysis said in an X post that Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 next-generation AI server rack system has been delayed by more than a year, citing setbacks in the construction of printed circuit boards for the platform; the item does not date the post and states that Nvidia did not respond t\",\n     \"Research firm SemiAnalysis said in an X post that Nvidia's next-generation AI server rack system, Kyber NVL144, has been delayed by more than a year due to manufacturing difficulties, specifically setbacks in the construction of printed circuit boards for the platform. Nvidia did not respond to a re\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"SemiAnalysis, in a thread on X, reported that Nvidia will not ship its Kyber NVL144 rack until 2028 — a delay of more than 12 months that pushes the cabinet meant for 2027's Rubin Ultra GPUs into the following year — with the holdup ostensibly caused by manufacturing challenges with a PCB midplane (\",\n     \"Per SemiAnalysis, Nvidia killed NVL72x2 — a stopgap rack that would have bolted two Oberon racks back-to-back to reach Kyber-class density over copper NVLink — after its largest customers balked at running two linked cabinets as a single unit, leaving, according to the report, no proven alternative \",\n     \"The report said NVL576 — a separate configuration tying eight racks together through co-packaged optics — is likely to slip or ship in low volume until that optical technology matures.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Delays Next-Generation Kyber Server Architecture as Manufacturing Hurdles Give Rivals a Rare Opening\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Research firm SemiAnalysis reported that Nvidia's Kyber rack-scale server design — built to pack 144 of Nvidia's most powerful chips into a single cabinet and originally due to launch alongside Vera Rubin Ultra in 2027 — has been pushed back more than a year, from 2027 to 2028. SemiAnalysis attribut\",\n     \"SemiAnalysis reported that NVL576, the larger version of Nvidia's Kyber design that links eight racks together via optical connections, is also likely to be delayed or to ship only in small volumes.\",\n     \"Nvidia's backup plan for scaling Rubin Ultra — bolting two current-generation racks together to reach similar compute power — was scrapped after cloud customers reportedly rejected it as awkward to operate and expensive to run, according to SemiAnalysis, leaving Nvidia without a proven way to scale \"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia underperforms peers as report sparks rack delay worries\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Supply-chain research firm SemiAnalysis alleged in a weekend report that Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 rack architecture will be delayed to 2028 because of manufacturing challenges with its PCB midplane, as reported by Investing.com.\",\n     \"SemiAnalysis further alleged, in the weekend report cited by Investing.com, that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\",\n     \"SemiAnalysis's weekend report also pointed to a downsized version of Nvidia's upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, alleging that a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped, per Investing.com.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"input_id\": \"gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"A Circuit Board Problem Just Delayed Nvidia's Next AI System to 2028 And Chip Stocks Are Already Feeling the Fallout\",\n    \"statements\": [\n     \"Semiconductor research firm SemiAnalysis reported on July 5–6, 2026 (a post CNBC cited) that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale AI system has been delayed from a planned 2027 launch to 2028. SemiAnalysis attributed the delay to manufacturing difficulty with the system's PCB midplane (orthogonal backpl\",\n     \"NVIDIA publicly disputed SemiAnalysis's report of a Kyber NVL144 delay, with a spokesperson telling Bloomberg that the company's \\\"roadmap is intact.\\\"\",\n     \"Semiconductor research firm SemiAnalysis reported on July 5–6, 2026 that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale AI system has been delayed from a planned 2027 launch to 2028, with the gating item being the PCB midplane (orthogonal backplane), a printed circuit board of up to 78 layers that SemiAnalysis sa\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n }\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
